cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "Code and paper for: The dark companion of J0008+0128 need not be a supermassive neutron star"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Paper and code for a Research Note of the AAS commenting on Zhao et al. (2026,
  Science Advances, 12, eaeg3307) about the red giant plus dark companion binary
  J0008+0128. j0008_analysis.py reproduces every number in the note and its figure
  from the values in inputs.csv; j0008_hrd.py gives the MIST track masses.
authors:
  - given-names: Simon
    family-names: Stevenson
    affiliation: "Centre for Astrophysics and Supercomputing, Swinburne University of Technology"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6100-537X"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24293381
repository-code: "https://github.com/SimonStevenson/j0008-rnaas"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - neutron stars
  - stellar masses
  - binary stars
  - Gaia
